<title>UK: Statoil announces Froy gas tender for 540,000 th/d.</title>
<headline>Statoil announces Froy gas tender for 540,000 th/d.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statoil's Alliance Gas confirmed on Friday that Statoil Norway has announced a tender for Froy natural gas landing at St Fergus in Scotland from October.</p>
<p>A trader at Alliance in London confirmed that three blocks of gas -- respectively 270,000 therms a day (th/d), 180,000 th/d and 90,000 th/d -- are offered either for the fourth quarter only or for the gas year starting in October.</p>
<p>Norway's state-owned Statoil (Den Norske Stats Oljeselskap ASA) holds 72 percent of Froy, Total SA 20 percent and Norsk Hydro ASA eight percent, the trader said.</p>
<p>Spot prices in the U.K. softened on Friday afternoon in response to the news, the trader added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
